k-arts platform-nantes 2025 international exchange workshops results exhibition ≪mon sens garde 몽상가들≫

≪mon sens garde 몽상가들≫, a 2025 joint international exchange workshop results exhibition by k-arts platform-nantes, is inspired by the perspective that the sense of &amp;ldquo;reverie&amp;rdquo; forms the minimal unit and ignition point for perceiving the world. distinguished from imagination or dream with which we are familiar, the concept of reverie refers to the most intrinsic level of perception &amp;ndash; one that shapes and judges the sense of reality through intimate contact with the external world. through acts of crossing, colliding, and transforming, multiple senses bring us to the threshold of a potential reality that lies beyond our accustomed knowledge and fixed frameworks. this exhibition contends that such dynamics &amp;ndash; the subtle vibrations between reverie and reality &amp;ndash; constitute essential conditions for critical thinking, revealing how perceptual shifts emerge in the spaces they create.

the exhibition presents outcomes from a photography workshop employing large-format film cameras, collaborative works from an improvisational narrative video and sound workshop, and individual artworks developed through each artist&amp;rsquo;s independent research. works by kim young hyun, jung hee jae, tunalee, ines de la torre gaspar barbosa, and sakari kyyr&amp;ouml;nen each pursue distinct pathways of sensory experience to mediate the external world. while deconstructing and reconstructing structures derived from reality, these works generate new inquiries.

