  $str$490$str$,
  $str$Hangeul Font Designs$str$,
  $str$국립한글박물관$str$,
  $str$Hangeul Nanum Madang(The Na & Da)$str$,
  null,
  $str$<h6>Introduction</h6>  The National Hangeul Museum holds a special exhibition titled Hangeul Font Designs. With the help of design, the value of letters can be enhanced from something that is used to read and write into something that can be felt and experienced. This exhibition is presented to shed light on the role of Hangeul font designs in the country’s cultural industry over the past 30 years, and on the diversity of such designs. In this exhibition, the visitors are invited to learn the role of Hangeul font designs in modern cultural industry by looking at the use of original hand-drawn images of letters to make printing types and by looking at how font designs have been developed.It is hoped that visitors will be able to appreciate the true values of Hangeul font designs through the exhibition. <h6 style="margin-top: 30px;">1. Changes in Printing Types</h6>  A font for types refers to a font for printing types which is a set of characters in certain style and size in order to improve legibility. In the olden days, printing types were made of wood or metal. Their producers experienced various difficulties depending on the nature of the materials used. With the onset of the early modern period, printing types began to be made with lead, later on, with the introduction of the matrix cutting machine, they were made using original hand-drawn images of letters. Hand-drawn letters were also used in a photocomposing machine. Later, it became the basis of the modern digital printing type production method. The shift in the method of producing printing types to the use of hand-drawn letters marked a major turning point in font designs.  <h6>2. Development of Hangeul Font Designs</h6>  The rapid development of font designs in the era of digital printing types is due to the shift from tangible printing types to their intangible counterparts. As for Hangeul fonts, which require the production of 11,172 characters, diverse font designs could be developed within a short period of time thanks to the structure of Hangeul, in which the initial, medial and final sounds can be combined into syllabic character blocks. Outline fonts came to be used even with desktop computers by the late 1990s, which led to the rapid development of Hangeul font designs.  <h6>3. Hangeul Font Designs in the Cultural Industry</h6> Hangeul font designs are a basic element of the Hangeul-related cultural industry. Especially they are widely used in such areas as application of traditional fonts, combination with other contents and culture-based social activities.Exclusive fonts are font designs made for a specific purpose such as enhancing the readability of electronic books or marketing tools for various items.Font designs used to be developed only by font businesses, but now individual designers can also take part in the production of font designs due to improved technologies, such as the advent of new software tools that enables developing a new design with less efforts.  <h6>Photo</h6><!-- tab -->    <h5 class="subTabCmu1"></h5>    <h5 class="subTabCmu2"></h5>    <h5 class="subTabCmu3"></h5>    <h5 class="subTabCmu4"></h5>    <h5 class="subTabCmu5"></h5>    <h5 class="subTabCmu6"></h5>    <h5 class="subTabCmu7"></h5>    <h5 class="subTabCmu8"></h5>    <h5 class="subTabCmu9"></h5>    <h5 class="subTabCmu10"></h5>    <h5 class="subTabCmu11"></h5>    <h5 class="subTabCmu12"></h5>    <h5 class="subTabCmu13"></h5>    <h5 class="subTabCmu14"></h5>    <h5 class="subTabCmu15"></h5>   <!--// tab --> <!-- #program_preview{display:inline-block;margin:30px 0;font-family:NanumGothic,나눔고딕,나눔 고딕,맑은 고딕,dotum;font-size:12px;} #program_preview > .poster_img{float:left;display:inline-block;margin-right:20px;width:298px;} #program_preview > .description {float:right;overflow:hidden;width:370px;} #program_preview > .description li {border-bottom:1px solid #ccc} #program_preview > .description li .stitle{font-weight:bold;color:#355b78;background-color: #fff;} #program_previ